      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Corners%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Upper Long Branch of Four Mile Run runs through the northernmost part of the community, and the adjacent land is slated for phased development by the Fairfax County Park Authority.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Corners%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Seven Corners sits on Munson's Hill, overlooking Upton's Hill and offering unbroken views toward Annandale and Fairfax City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
